==================================================
CORE BEHAVIOR SCORING ENGINE
==================================================

export function scoreBehavior(
  input: BehaviorInput
): BehaviorScore {

  const reasons: string[] = [];

  let score = 0;

  const window =
    input.launchWindowSeconds ?? 5;

  if (
    input.secondsFromLaunch !== null &&
    input.secondsFromLaunch <= window
  ) {
    score += 35;

    reasons.push(
      `trade occurred within ${window}s opening window`
    );
  }

  if (
    input.inferredSnipeFee > 0n
  ) {
    score += 35;

    reasons.push(
      "trade paid fee above estimated base fee, consistent with opening snipe tax"
    );
  }

  if (
    (input.priorOpeningLaunches ?? 0) >= 3
  ) {
    score += 30;

    reasons.push(
      "recipient has repeated opening-window participation across at least 3 launches"
    );
  }

  if (
    score >= 80
  ) {
    return {
      classification:
        "automated-candidate",

      score,

      reasons
    };
  }

  if (
    score >= 35
  ) {
    return {
      classification:
        "opening-window",

      score,

      reasons
    };
  }

  return {
    classification:
      "ordinary",

    score,

    reasons
  };
}

==================================================
SCORING LOGIC
==================================================

SIGNAL 1

OPENING-WINDOW TIMING

If the transaction occurs within the configured launch window:

+35

This establishes:

EARLY PARTICIPATION.

It does not establish automation by itself.

SIGNAL 2

ADDITIONAL OPENING-WINDOW FEE

If the transaction contains a defensibly inferred opening-window fee component:

+35

This provides another independent protocol-level signal that the transaction interacted under opening-window conditions.

SIGNAL 3

REPEATED EARLY PARTICIPATION

If the same subject has participated inside the opening window of at least three prior launches:

+30

This strengthens evidence of recurring machine-like or systematic behavior.

==================================================
CURRENT CLASSIFICATION THRESHOLDS
==================================================

0–34

ORDINARY

The available signals do not justify an opening-window classification.

35–79

OPENING-WINDOW

The transaction exhibits one or more opening-window characteristics.

80–100

AUTOMATED-CANDIDATE

Multiple signals converge sufficiently to justify further automated-behavior research.

IMPORTANT:

AUTOMATED-CANDIDATE

DOES NOT MEAN:

AUTOMATION-CONFIRMED.

It means:

THE OBSERVED BEHAVIOR JUSTIFIES ADDITIONAL INVESTIGATION.

==================================================
WHY THE SCORE REQUIRES MULTIPLE SIGNALS
==================================================

A transaction occurring quickly after launch may simply reflect:

a human watching the protocol,
a public indexing service,
a notification system,
a trader already monitoring the factory,
or ordinary coincidence.

Therefore timing alone produces:

OPENING-WINDOW

rather than:

AUTOMATED-CANDIDATE.

The stronger classification requires convergence.

